### Phase 3A — storage + create post
### Set @token from phase1/http-client.env.json after login.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@token = paste-user-access-token-here

### 1. Create a SELL post with 2 images  -> 201
###    Use the "Select Files" action IntelliJ shows on each < ./path line.
POST {{host}}/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="post"
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Used calculus textbook",
  "description": "Lightly used, no highlights in the first ten chapters.",
  "categoryId": 1,
  "listingType": "SELL",
  "price": 450.00,
  "condition": "GOOD"
}
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="images"; filename="cover.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./test-images/cover.jpg
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="images"; filename="back.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./test-images/back.jpg
--WebAppBoundary--

### 2. Create an EXCHANGE post, no images  -> 201
POST {{host}}/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="post"
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Scientific calculator swap",
  "description": "Want to trade my FX-991 for a graphing calculator.",
  "categoryId": 2,
  "listingType": "EXCHANGE",
  "exchangeWanted": "Graphing calculator",
  "condition": "LIKE_NEW"
}
--WebAppBoundary--

### 3. FREE post with a price  -> 400 (db price-consistency rule)
POST {{host}}/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="post"
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Free study guides",
  "description": "Giving away my first-year study guides.",
  "categoryId": 1,
  "listingType": "FREE",
  "price": 10,
  "condition": "FAIR"
}
--WebAppBoundary--

### 4. SELL with no price  -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="post"
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Desk lamp for sale",
  "description": "Working desk lamp, minor scratch on the base.",
  "categoryId": 3,
  "listingType": "SELL",
  "condition": "GOOD"
}
--WebAppBoundary--

### 5. Renamed .exe uploaded as .jpg  -> 400 (magic bytes, not filename)
POST {{host}}/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="post"
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Suspicious upload",
  "description": "This file is not really a JPEG image.",
  "categoryId": 1,
  "listingType": "SELL",
  "price": 1,
  "condition": "GOOD"
}
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="images"; filename="not-an-image.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./test-images/not-an-image.exe
--WebAppBoundary--

### 6. Six images  -> 400 (max 5)
###    Repeat the images part six times with different files.

### 7. Inactive or unknown category  -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="post"
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Unknown category post",
  "description": "The category id below does not exist.",
  "categoryId": 999999,
  "listingType": "SELL",
  "price": 5,
  "condition": "GOOD"
}
--WebAppBoundary--

### 8. No token  -> 401
POST {{host}}/api/posts
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="post"
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Unauthenticated post",
  "description": "Should never reach the service layer.",
  "categoryId": 1,
  "listingType": "SELL",
  "price": 5,
  "condition": "GOOD"
}
--WebAppBoundary--

### 9. Rate limit: run request #1 four times quickly  -> 4th returns 429
###    (3/min per user, separate from the 10/day window)

### 10. Oversized image (> 5 MB)  -> 413
###     Any valid JPEG larger than 5 MB triggers MaxUploadSizeExceededException.